TEXT 0 -420 Left 2 ;Lab C - condenser microphones 4133 / 4134 excited by an electrostatic actuator (pressure applied directly to the diaphragm, no T(s) block)
TEXT 0 -388 Left 2 ;left: ACOUSTIC, impedance analogy (V = pressure, I = volume velocity)   middle: MECHANICAL, mobility analogy (V = diaphragm velocity, I = force)   right: ELECTRICAL (V(out) = open-circuit output per Pa)
TEXT 0 -340 Left 2 !.param a=0.004475 x0=2.077e-05 E=200 MMD=1.5e-06 CMD=2e-05 Vb=1.264e-07 RL=1e+10 rho=1.18 c=344.0
TEXT 0 -308 Left 2 !.param SD=pi*a**2 CAB=Vb/(rho*c**2) MA1=0.6133*rho/(pi*a) CMT=1/(1/CMD+SD**2/CAB) CE0=8.854e-12*SD/x0
TEXT 0 -176 Left 2 ;B&K 4133 (S/N 591628):  type the measured values here ->
TEXT 0 -144 Left 2 !.param fs33=20000 Q33=0.45
TEXT 0 -112 Left 2 !.param MMT33=1/((2*pi*fs33)**2*CMT) MAS33=(MMT33-MMD)/SD**2-MA1 RAS33=sqrt(MMT33/CMT)/Q33/SD**2
TEXT 1078 16 Left 1 ;actuator = 1 Pa on the diaphragm
TEXT 0 344 Left 2 ;B&K 4134 (S/N 1534527):  type the measured values here ->
TEXT 0 376 Left 2 !.param fs34=20000 Q34=0.95
TEXT 0 408 Left 2 !.param MMT34=1/((2*pi*fs34)**2*CMT) MAS34=(MMT34-MMD)/SD**2-MA1 RAS34=sqrt(MMT34/CMT)/Q34/SD**2
TEXT 1078 536 Left 1 ;actuator = 1 Pa on the diaphragm
TEXT 0 800 Left 2 !.ac dec 200 20 60k
TEXT 0 848 Left 2 ;plot V(out33) V(out34): magnitude in dB re 1 V/Pa and phase. Low-frequency level = E*SD*CMT/x0 = 11.1 mV/Pa (-39.1 dB), below the nominal 12.5 mV/Pa: see the appendix of the brief.
TEXT 0 880 Left 2 ;fs = where the phase has dropped 90 deg from its mid-band value,  Q = |H(fs)| / |H(f << fs)| (linear).  A 180 deg offset against the measurement is only the ground convention.
